  "facts": [
    "Both entered and completed a real process with the original generation; both collected zero nodes and settled exactly their own run.",
    "Both explicit search calls returned attempted:false / visible-opponent-too-close. No E search channel started in these runs.",
    "No body-route exception, stuck movement assertion or navigationWarning was recorded; complete return succeeded for seed3075192741. This does not establish all possible routes are safe.",
    "The frozen policy excludes near-entry nodes <=320px, follows one far terrain direction, defers unsafe observed targets, then returns on health/chaos/distance thresholds. These are limitations of the test driver, not additional game rules.",
    "Seed20261005 died on the retreat with actual nearby pursuing enemies; seed3075192741 returned alive with55HP. Both misses are gameplay/controller outcomes rather than network failures."
  ],
  "inference": "Evidence demonstrates failure of these two exact controller processes, not impossibility of the authored world. A route/policy limitation is plausible because both refuse to start search after threat observation, but alternative safe player inputs are untested. No product fix or changed control policy is justified solely by this diagnosis.",
  "qualification": "white-scarfield severe remains unqualified: original two seeds contain no non-entry search-and-extract. Preserve loss/empty-return and request root decision before any additional probe."
}
